    "title": "Food exposed to floodwater discard boundary",
    "category": "Practical · Emergency · Expansion",
    "subcategory": "Flood · Food · Safety",
    "summary": "Separate anything touched by floodwater, sewage, chemicals, damaged packaging, rust, swelling, leakage, or broken seals.",
    "content": "Discard unsafe items according to official food-safety guidance and document losses for aid or insurance. Do not wash and reuse food in cardboard, cloth, screw-top, snap-lid, or damaged containers after flood exposure.",
